# ...except the template, which documents every variable and holds no values.
!.env.example

# OS / editors
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
.claude/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Data.
#
# The real curriculum corpus is private and is NOT part of this repository.
# Only data/sample/ (synthetic, generated for this repo) is tracked — it is
# what lets anyone clone this and run the whole pipeline.
#
# The unanchored rule below is deliberate: it matches the private corpus
# wherever it lands, so a stray copy in a scratch folder can never be
# committed by an absent-minded `git add .`.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
quizzes-raw-data.json
**/quizzes-raw-data.json

data/raw/
data/interim/
data/processed/
data/vector_store/
data/sample/interim/
data/sample/processed/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Eval inputs and outputs.
#
# The ground-truth files are DERIVED FROM THE PRIVATE CORPUS: each test case
# carries a real `target_quiz_title`, and the topics CSVs map those titles to
# real doc_ids. No personal data, but it is private curriculum content and it
# does not belong in a public repository.
#
# eval/RESULTS.md is the deliberate exception — aggregate metrics only, no
# corpus content — and is tracked.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
eval/*.json
eval/*.csv
eval/results/

# Generated at runtime
logs/
last_run.json
